# Environment variables for the Next app. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Nothing here is required. Every variable has a defined behaviour when unset,
# because a developer cloning this repo should get a working site rather than a
# stack trace, and because half of these point at services that do not exist
# yet. What each one does when it is missing is written next to it.
#
# Added 24 August 2026, with the Strapi integration. Until then the variables
# below were documented only in the comments of the files that read them, which
# is not somewhere anybody looks before their first run.

# The site's own origin. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, the sitemap
# and every schema block, all of which have to be absolute.
#
# Unset: falls back to https://www.hitasoft.com, which is correct for production
# and wrong for a preview deployment. Set this on previews so they point at
# themselves rather than at the live site. See content/site.ts, and note that
# the value has to match the host that actually serves the page, since the
# apex 301s to www at the edge.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Google Analytics 4. Added 25 August 2026, replacing @vercel/analytics, which
# only ever worked on Vercel and 404'd on this droplet.
#
# Unset: falls back to the property's real measurement ID, hardcoded in
# components/analytics/google-analytics.tsx. That is deliberate rather than
# sloppy: the ID ships in the HTML of every page anyway, so it is not a
# secret, and a value that lives only in a deployment environment is one
# nobody can find later.
#
# Set it to point a staging deploy at a different property. Set it to an
# empty string to turn analytics off for a deploy entirely.
#
# Nothing loads outside NODE_ENV=production either way, so `pnpm dev` never
# files itself as real traffic.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# Where Strapi is, and a token to read it with.
#
# Unset: the site serves the ten sample posts in content/posts-sample.ts and
# renders exactly as it did before the CMS existed. See lib/strapi.ts, and
# cms/README.md for how to generate the token.
#
# The token must be Read-only. The site never writes, and a read only token
# limits the damage if one ever reaches a log. Neither variable is NEXT_PUBLIC,
# so neither reaches a browser.
STRAPI_URL=http://localhost:1337
STRAPI_API_TOKEN=

# Where the contact form's submissions actually go. Two channels, checked in
# this order — see app/api/contact/route.ts for the full explanation.
#
# Resend, preferred: emails the submission to CONTACT_TO_EMAIL. Needs
# hitasoft.com verified as a sending domain in the Resend dashboard first.
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=   # optional, defaults to "Hitasoft site <contact@hitasoft.com>"
#   CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=    # optional, defaults to info@hitasoft.com
#
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL, fallback: a JSON POST to any provider that takes one —
# Zapier, Make, n8n, a Slack incoming webhook. Used only when RESEND_API_KEY
# is not set.
#
# Both unset: /api/contact returns a 503 with an honest message rather than
# pretending to deliver anything.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Where the quote assistant's enquiries go. Added 27 August 2026.
#
# /api/quote uses the same RESEND_API_KEY and RESEND_FROM_EMAIL above — these
# two only change the destination, so quote requests can be routed somewhere
# different from general contact form traffic.
#
# QUOTE_TO_EMAIL unset: falls back to CONTACT_TO_EMAIL, then to
# info@hitasoft.com. QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL unset: falls back to
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL. Set neither and quote requests land wherever contact
# form submissions already do, which is the sane default.
#
# Note the webhook path names an attached document rather than carrying it —
# posting 11MB of base64 at a Slack hook is how you break a Slack hook. Resend
# is the channel that actually delivers the file.
QUOTE_TO_EMAIL=
QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# The quote assistant's grounded answering, behind the "Something else" branch
# of the modal. Added 27 August 2026.
#
# Unset: that option goes straight to the brief step instead of opening the
# assistant. A working path rather than a degraded one, and the same rule as
# everything above — a missing key means a feature is absent, never a wall
# somebody hits.
#
# Server side only, and it has to stay that way. This is NOT NEXT_PUBLIC: a
# key in the browser is a key anybody can spend. app/api/quote/ask/route.ts is
# the only thing that reads it, and the browser talks to that route.
#
# Generate one at console.anthropic.com, under API keys.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare Turnstile, the contact form's spam check beyond the honeypot.
# Added 24 August 2026. The site key is NEXT_PUBLIC because the widget needs
# it in the browser; the secret key never leaves the server.
#
# Unset (either one): the widget does not render and the server skips
# verification rather than rejecting every submission nobody can pass. Set
# both together, never just one. Generate a pair in the Cloudflare dashboard
# under Turnstile, widget mode "Managed".
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# The quote assistant's archive and its conversational state. Added 27 August
# 2026, extended the same day when the assistant became a real conversation.
#
# Unset: nothing is recorded, /admin says so plainly, and — since the
# conversational assistant's phase lives in this database rather than in the
# browser — QuoteBot itself falls back to the scripted question flow instead
# of opening a chat window it has nowhere to remember state for. See lib/db.ts
# and lib/quote-store.ts for why an unset value degrades rather than crashes.
#
# Needs one `pnpm db:migrate` run before the first deploy that includes this.
DATABASE_URL=

# ADMIN_USER / ADMIN_PASSWORD: basic auth on /admin and /api/admin. Unlike
# everything else on this page, an unset pair does NOT mean "feature absent" —
# it means nobody gets in, ever. See the shouted note on this in proxy.ts.
ADMIN_USER=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Where uploaded requirement documents are written. Added 27 August 2026.
#
# Unset: falls back to .uploads/ next to the project, which is fine for
# development and WRONG for the server — see the shouted note in
# lib/quote-uploads.ts. On the droplet this has to be a path on a Docker
# volume, or every redeploy takes the uploads with it and an estimate job
# fails trying to read a file that is simply gone.
QUOTE_UPLOAD_DIR=

# A pepper mixed into the OTP code hash, on top of the per-code random salt.
# Added 27 August 2026. See lib/quote-otp.ts for what this does and does not
# protect against.
#
# Unset: the salt alone still does the necessary work — this is a second
# layer, not the only one. Set it in production; there is no reason not to.
OTP_PEPPER=

# Which model writes the estimate itself, once a conversation finishes. Added
# 27 August 2026. See lib/quote-estimate.ts for why this is a different model
# from QUOTE_MODEL below — this one has to reason, and it runs once per lead
# rather than once per turn, so the cost of a larger model barely registers.
#
# Unset: falls back to claude-sonnet-5.
QUOTE_ESTIMATE_MODEL=

# The bearer secret on POST /api/quote/estimate/run, which drains the estimate
# queue. Added 27 August 2026. See the shouted note in that route: unlike
# every other variable on this page, unset here means the endpoint REFUSES
# rather than opening — it spends money on every call, so there is no safe
# "absent means off" reading for a missing secret.
#
# Point a schedule at the route with this as a bearer token, every ten minutes
# or so. Generate any long random string.
QUOTE_CRON_SECRET=

# Overrides the model behind the conversational assistant. Added 27 August
# 2026. See the note on MODEL in app/api/quote/chat/route.ts for why this
# stays on Haiku rather than following QUOTE_ESTIMATE_MODEL upmarket.
#
# Unset: falls back to claude-haiku-4-5.
QUOTE_MODEL=
